    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nFix MFSDP v2's wrapping of `ShortcutMoEBlock`. The block calls its attention layer's two-stage methods and its MoE layer/MLP's routing methods directly, bypassing their `__call__` hooks. Wrapping those layers separately leaves their parameters sharded when shortcut execution accesses them; wrapping only their parent cannot gather parameters already owned by child FSDP units.\n\nMake the shortcut block the FSDP unit for these parameters, and exclude its directly invoked attention layer, MoE layer, and MoE MLP from child-unit selection. Experts retain their separate expert-DP units. Other explicitly selected children, such as norms invoked through `__call__`, can still be units.\n\nStacked on #7809, reusing its real `HybridModel` EP test and process-group fixtures. This diff switches the shortcut cases from explicit block-only wrapping to automatic wrapping, including broad explicit child selection. All six preceding variants retain prefetch, five-step loss parity, overlap/recomputation coverage, and ownership/mesh assertions.\n\n## Validation\n\nRestacked on #7809 on October 13. Syntax, Black, isort, and Ruff pass; GPU validation of this restacked head is pending.\n\nEarlier revision `0d72b5ca4` passed three adapter cases on each of four GPU ranks. Its explicit-norm case disabled prefetch. The current stack includes #7809's ordering fix and keeps prefetch enabled, so those earlier results do not validate the new combined test configuration.\n\n## Contribution checks\n\n- [x] Relevant unit tests\n- [ ] Functional tests\n- [x] Relevant API documentation\n- [x] Repository formatter and lint checks\n\nNo GPU kernels or numerical operators are changed.\n",
